file: shell.cpp
---

# shell tool

Executes shell scripts natively. --run and -c parse with the project's own
parser and evaluate through mm.shell.full over the mm.shell.posix host
services; nothing here calls system() and nothing reaches /bin/sh unless
--legacy-sh is given explicitly. --check, --tokens, and --dump-ast are
parser-only modes, --capabilities and --commands are introspection, and
--profile=embedded runs the bounded embedded evaluator instead.

--legacy-sh is a deprecated one-release rollback that delegates to /bin/sh
through the process service. It is never selected automatically after a native
parse or execution failure, prints a deprecation diagnostic, and cannot be
combined with --profile=embedded. The [manifest] command positional form is a
deprecated alias for -c that uses the native parser.
